WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.812 --> 01:30.732
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.651 --> 01:33.986
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.862 --> 01:35.905
Black Jack.

01:48.867 --> 01:52.034
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "An Amazing Tongue"

01:48.867 --> 01:52.034
An Abacus Prodigy

02:12.398 --> 02:14.733
Here you go.

02:17.153 --> 02:19.201
Sharaku-kun, are you studying?

02:19.488 --> 02:20.488
Good for you.

02:20.489 --> 02:25.535
My sister won't stop telling me to do my homework
and I don't like her constant nagging.

02:26.078 --> 02:27.996
She never changes.

02:34.378 --> 02:36.421
It's so cold!

02:38.674 --> 02:40.896
That was yummy.

02:41.052 --> 02:44.929
Your Pinoco Special is the best.

02:48.517 --> 02:50.000
What's that?

02:50.853 --> 02:51.978
This?

02:52.271 --> 02:53.938
This is an abacus.

02:54.137 --> 02:55.715
An abacus?

02:55.928 --> 02:57.281
An abacus.

02:57.860 --> 03:00.570
It's a tool for arithmetic that came from China.

03:00.571 --> 03:04.756
It's thought to have come to Japan around the 1570s.

03:05.034 --> 03:08.078
Also, August 8th is the official day of the abacus.

03:08.079 --> 03:08.912
The reason is

03:08.913 --> 03:10.163
because it sounds like "pachi, pachi."

03:08.913 --> 03:10.173
Note: "pachi pachi" is the sound imitation of an abacus
and also a way to pronounce the number eight.

03:13.393 --> 03:15.210
You know a lot.

03:16.337 --> 03:19.172
Sharaku's no good with school subjects,

03:19.173 --> 03:21.674
but he knows a lot of weird stuff.

03:23.469 --> 03:25.011
I don't know that much...

03:25.012 --> 03:28.473
You should start using a calculator.

03:28.474 --> 03:29.945
Don't say that.

03:30.142 --> 03:32.852
Abaci work just fine.

03:32.853 --> 03:35.271
Once you get used to them, you can do
any kind of arithmetic with them,

03:35.272 --> 03:36.815
and you get real good at calculating in your head.

03:36.816 --> 03:38.858
You think faster too.

03:39.033 --> 03:40.819
Ohmigewdness!

03:40.820 --> 03:43.404
You get smarter if you use an abacus?

03:43.406 --> 03:44.606
Yes, you do.

03:44.693 --> 03:46.093
I'll use it too!

03:47.201 --> 03:50.568
Let me borrow it!

03:47.868 --> 03:50.568
Hey now, I'm still using it.

03:52.498 --> 03:53.331
Doc?

03:53.332 --> 03:54.634
Is something wrong?

03:56.043 --> 03:57.924
No, it's nothing.

03:59.421 --> 04:00.672
<i>Abaci, huh?</i>

04:09.682 --> 04:10.890
My name's Muraoka.

04:11.475 --> 04:12.809
This is my son, Eiji.

04:14.562 --> 04:17.188
This is Eiji's teacher.

04:17.189 --> 04:18.314
I'm Saeki.

04:18.315 --> 04:20.567
Thank you for seeing us.

04:21.026 --> 04:23.903
I haven't even given you my opinion yet.

04:23.904 --> 04:25.280
Anyway, come on in.

04:28.742 --> 04:30.410
Ectrodactyly?

04:30.411 --> 04:30.935
Yes.

04:31.328 --> 04:33.424
He hasn't been able to use his fingers since birth.

04:33.581 --> 04:36.760
Please heal his hands.

04:37.585 --> 04:39.836
You didn't have to come to me for that.

04:39.837 --> 04:42.264
You should go see another doctor.

04:42.715 --> 04:44.882
It'll be much cheaper that way.

04:45.509 --> 04:46.426
Please leave.

04:48.637 --> 04:51.139
It has to be you.

04:51.599 --> 04:54.638
Eiji-kun's very talented with the abacus.

04:55.102 --> 04:58.396
He's even mastered calculations at the junior high level.

04:58.397 --> 05:01.149
In order for him to retain the level
he's at and grow further,

05:01.150 --> 05:04.944
| want you to give him the ability
to use an abacus with his hands.

05:06.030 --> 05:07.157
An abacus, huh?

05:09.867 --> 05:13.286
He's been using another part of his body up until now.

05:13.787 --> 05:14.829
Watch.

05:15.247 --> 05:16.627
Go for it, Eiji-kun.

05:19.001 --> 05:20.752
What is 3,253

05:20.753 --> 05:22.522
plus 5,407

05:22.559 --> 05:24.519
plus 2,651

05:24.579 --> 05:26.471
plus 4,177

05:26.645 --> 05:28.633
plus 3,959

05:28.927 --> 05:31.304
plus 4,178?

05:31.930 --> 05:34.307
23,625.

05:34.975 --> 05:36.225
That's right!

05:37.020 --> 05:38.020
See?

05:38.187 --> 05:39.880
Wasn't that wonderful?

05:41.857 --> 05:44.734
Why do you need fingers when you can already do that?

05:45.861 --> 05:50.698
Everyone laughs at me when I use an abacus like this.

05:51.367 --> 05:53.910
If they laugh at you, laugh back.

05:54.244 --> 06:00.281
If he gives up the abacus now, his life will be ruined.

06:01.085 --> 06:03.211
Please, Dr. Black Jack!

06:06.340 --> 06:11.094
Even if I operate on him, I can't guarantee he'll
ever be able to use an abacus normally.

06:11.428 --> 06:14.081
I've seen your previous work.

06:14.348 --> 06:16.057
I believe in you.

06:16.850 --> 06:18.518
Also, it'll cost you.

06:23.065 --> 06:24.618
I have ¥10,000,000 here.

06:24.942 --> 06:27.485
I've been saving it up so his hands could be fixed.

06:29.613 --> 06:30.530
That's not enough.

06:30.948 --> 06:32.198
I need ¥30,000,000.

06:32.991 --> 06:34.699
¥30,000,000?!

06:36.232 --> 06:37.316
No way.

06:37.317 --> 06:40.110
I have ¥10,000,000 in my savings account.

06:41.446 --> 06:42.994
Miss Saeki...

06:43.448 --> 06:46.617
I want Eiji-kun to continue improving his abacus abilities.

06:47.285 --> 06:49.787
But you're still ¥10,000,000 short.

06:51.790 --> 06:54.638
I'll become so good with the abacus that I'll become the national champion, and then I'll pay you back.

06:54.959 --> 06:57.086
Do you even know what you're saying, Eiji?

06:57.087 --> 07:00.005
Even if you do become the champion
you won't be able to pay for it.

07:02.092 --> 07:05.578
So, you're going to become the best
in the nation if I fix your hands?

07:08.932 --> 07:11.253
You'll have to endure a difficult and painful
rehabilitation after they're fixed.

07:13.770 --> 07:15.813
I'm going to do it.

07:22.195 --> 07:23.768
Let's examine your fingers.

07:24.322 --> 07:25.739
Enter the x-ray room.

07:28.535 --> 07:29.326
Then...

07:30.411 --> 07:32.079
The operation will be a week from today.

07:35.625 --> 07:37.084
Thank you very much.

07:39.437 --> 07:43.564
One Week Later

07:59.148 --> 08:00.440
Let me tell you something before we start.

08:00.441 --> 08:04.939
Even if his hands are fixed, his fingers will
never work like a normal person's.

08:05.446 --> 08:08.972
If he uses them for an extended period of time,
his fingers may stop working altogether,

08:09.284 --> 08:10.591
Please keep that in mind.

08:12.090 --> 08:13.078
Yes.

08:15.665 --> 08:16.564
Are you ready?

08:16.791 --> 08:17.471
Yes.

08:17.625 --> 08:19.543
Where's my abacus?

08:21.671 --> 08:23.213
Can I take it with me?

08:23.214 --> 08:24.298
I don't mind.

08:32.473 --> 08:34.099
Do you like the abacus that much?

08:35.476 --> 08:38.070
I like the sound of it.

08:38.354 --> 08:38.937
The sound?

08:38.938 --> 08:42.608
The sound of an abacus being used
reminds me of my dad's voice.

08:49.324 --> 08:51.867
My mom died when I was born.

08:52.019 --> 08:55.078
My dad took care of me even though he was working.

08:56.706 --> 08:57.539
Good.

08:58.166 --> 08:59.166
Thanks for waiting.

08:59.792 --> 09:00.756
Here you go.

09:01.878 --> 09:02.502
Enjoy.

09:05.131 --> 09:06.733
On nights when I had trouble sleeping,

09:07.008 --> 09:12.150
hearing the sound of the abacus in the
next room put me right to sleep.

09:13.598 --> 09:17.078
The sound of my dad using an abacus was like a lullaby.

09:19.062 --> 09:23.523
The abacus he gave me is my most important possession.

09:23.983 --> 09:26.042
That's enough talking for now.

09:26.444 --> 09:27.736
I'm going to give you an anesthetic.

09:28.196 --> 09:28.945
OK.

10:05.775 --> 10:08.150
<i>My abacus.</i>

10:32.975 --> 10:33.928
Doctor.

10:34.184 --> 10:35.194
How'd it go?

10:35.894 --> 10:38.184
I gave him five fingers.

10:38.522 --> 10:40.022
Now we'll have how the rehabilitation goes.

10:40.023 --> 10:40.898
Doctor.

10:40.899 --> 10:42.150
Thank you very much.

10:42.234 --> 10:43.526
Thank you very much.

10:47.281 --> 10:51.117
Doctor, Eiji-kun will put his hands to good use.

10:52.452 --> 10:54.475
Muraoka-san, this is great.

10:54.788 --> 10:55.663
Thank you.

10:55.956 --> 10:57.999
This really makes me happy.

11:00.836 --> 11:02.170
Miss Saeki.

11:04.329 --> 11:06.390
Muraoka-san what are you doing that for?

11:06.675 --> 11:11.470
Thank you so much for everything you've done for him.

11:11.471 --> 11:14.432
I just couldn't leave him alone.

11:15.601 --> 11:19.132
It's only because you were with
us that we could come this far.

11:19.479 --> 11:22.417
Please stay with my son from now on too.

11:25.527 --> 11:26.819
Muraoka-san...

11:38.707 --> 11:39.665
Eiji-kun!

11:40.167 --> 11:41.709
I can't move my fingers.

11:43.629 --> 11:47.381
Every time I try to move them they
hurt-almost like someone's twisting them.

11:49.092 --> 11:51.594
I can't use an abacus like this.

11:53.388 --> 11:57.808
Dr. Black Jack said it would be tough.

11:57.809 --> 12:01.710
Not even Dr. Black Jack knows how tough it really is!

12:01.939 --> 12:03.022
Eiji-kun!

12:17.621 --> 12:18.788
Miss Saeki!

12:40.519 --> 12:41.060
Eiji!

12:42.396 --> 12:44.402
Dad, you don't have to fix the abacus.

12:44.940 --> 12:47.109
I can't use it anymore.

12:47.442 --> 12:49.337
If you can't, you don't have to.

12:49.903 --> 12:54.193
I just wanted your hands fixed.

12:55.033 --> 12:56.922
But are you sure you're OK with that?

12:57.577 --> 12:59.177
Not really, but..

12:59.746 --> 13:02.540
Miss Saeki's worried about you.

13:03.250 --> 13:05.026
It's getting late, so go to bed.

13:05.335 --> 13:07.002
I'll have the abacus all fixed for you by tomorrow.

13:07.177 --> 13:08.963
It's your most important possession after all.

13:09.715 --> 13:11.465
It won't really get fixed.

13:11.466 --> 13:13.050
Just like my hands!

13:14.302 --> 13:15.008
Eiji!

13:19.282 --> 13:24.755
The Muraoka Restaurant

13:32.404 --> 13:34.029
It's fixed!

13:44.583 --> 13:46.333
I'm sorry, Dad.

13:47.002 --> 13:49.170
I'm sorry, Abacus-kun.

13:49.444 --> 13:52.059
I'm sorry for hurting you...

14:01.596 --> 14:02.335
Miss Saeki,

14:04.311 --> 14:07.271
would you teach me how to use an abacus again?

14:08.106 --> 14:08.856
Yes!

14:08.857 --> 14:10.159
Yes, of course!

14:10.317 --> 14:11.942
Let's work at it together.

14:27.751 --> 14:30.169
...and add 2,255?

14:30.462 --> 14:32.449
38,223.

14:32.756 --> 14:33.618
You're right!

14:33.798 --> 14:35.174
You did it, Eiji-kun!

14:40.013 --> 14:41.630
Dr. Black Jack,

14:42.015 --> 14:45.040
Eiji-kun will be participating in an abacus contest.

14:45.560 --> 14:50.189
I just wanted to let you know as I hope
you'll get to see him compete.

14:59.282 --> 15:03.035
What is 11,680,923

15:03.036 --> 15:06.787
plus 63,981,207

15:06.834 --> 15:10.354
plus 72,539,280

15:10.427 --> 15:13.917
plus 11,552,239

15:14.011 --> 15:17.607
plus 38,516,172

15:17.759 --> 15:21.543
plus 44,338,535?

15:28.812 --> 15:31.405
Muraoka Eiji will move on to the final round.

15:34.359 --> 15:37.653
We'll begin the final round after a ten minute break.

15:43.159 --> 15:45.959
Dr. Black Jack, you came!

15:46.329 --> 15:48.133
I received an invitation.

15:48.832 --> 15:52.741
Thanks to you, I get to participate in this contest.

15:53.128 --> 15:58.674
I'll win it just like I promised and
become the best in the nation!

16:02.804 --> 16:04.051
Dr. Black Jack.

16:04.347 --> 16:06.747
Thank you for coming.

16:07.058 --> 16:10.686
Eiji-kun said he wanted you to be there when he wins.

16:12.897 --> 16:14.523
It'll be difficult for him to win.

16:15.859 --> 16:18.844
Those fingers aren't able to to stand such
a large amount of physical activity yet.

16:19.320 --> 16:21.211
After about thirty minutes of use,
they'll be too sore to move.

16:21.823 --> 16:23.412
He used them for ten minutes during the quarter finals.

16:23.992 --> 16:25.396
Plus, he used them during the warm-ups.

16:26.035 --> 16:29.340
When you factor in the stress of being the
spotlight, which will tire them out faster,

16:29.789 --> 16:33.083
his fingers will stop functioning during the final round.

16:34.002 --> 16:36.795
Doctor, no way...

16:38.271 --> 16:44.136
We're now commencing the final round of the elementary
school division of the National Abacus Tournament.

16:44.429 --> 16:47.097
Begin problem one.

16:49.100 --> 16:50.254
It's the final round.

16:50.560 --> 16:52.144
I'm really going to do it.

16:52.270 --> 16:53.298
Ready.

16:53.563 --> 16:58.567
Please calculate 2,552,855...

17:02.805 --> 17:05.592
For problem one, both answered correctly.

17:06.201 --> 17:08.811
We'll now move on to problem two.

17:09.287 --> 17:10.204
Ready?

17:10.747 --> 17:15.834
Please calculate 5,854,339

17:15.835 --> 17:19.798
plus 97,621,458

17:20.006 --> 17:23.533
plus 43,295,408

17:20.046 --> 17:21.624
<i>Yes, good...</i>

17:22.192 --> 17:23.213
<i>Keep it up...</i>

17:23.246 --> 17:24.386
<i>Keep it up...</i>

17:23.559 --> 17:26.850
plus 40,746,455...

17:27.597 --> 17:29.187
<i>My fingers!</i>

17:29.474 --> 17:30.516
<i>What's wrong?</i>

17:30.517 --> 17:31.827
<i>It's getting hard to move them.</i>

17:32.310 --> 17:36.146
plus 28,966,141

17:36.147 --> 17:39.019
plus 37,000,028...

17:40.902 --> 17:41.684
Move!

17:42.153 --> 17:43.268
Move!

17:43.488 --> 17:47.449
plus 10,231,486.

17:49.494 --> 17:50.912
They're both correct.

17:51.287 --> 17:53.914
Now moving on to problem three...

17:54.457 --> 17:55.441
<i>I can't...</i>

17:55.917 --> 17:57.876
<i>I've come this far, but...</i>

17:57.877 --> 18:00.545
<i>I've practiced so much, but I can't do it!</i>

18:00.838 --> 18:03.298
Something's wrong with Eiji-kun.

18:03.800 --> 18:05.078
How can this be happening?!

18:05.468 --> 18:07.344
He's come so far, and yet...

18:11.099 --> 18:12.307
Ready?

18:16.562 --> 18:19.398
Are you ready, Muraoka-kun?

18:33.246 --> 18:34.246
<i>Dang it!</i>

18:37.208 --> 18:40.502
<i>I could only get this far because you were with me.</i>

18:40.962 --> 18:42.907
<i>How could I give up now?</i>

18:46.884 --> 18:48.135
Begin.

18:49.262 --> 18:54.057
Please add 46,173,152

18:54.252 --> 19:01.773
plus 63,391,86... 6--

19:02.567 --> 19:06.479
plus 63,295,581

19:06.654 --> 19:10.575
plus 92,260,553...

19:07.113 --> 19:09.480
Muraoka-san, Eiji-kun is...

19:10.575 --> 19:13.867
plus 81,333,780...

19:10.575 --> 19:10.975
Eiji!

19:13.940 --> 19:17.789
plus 73,444,116...

19:19.125 --> 19:20.000
Um...

19:20.334 --> 19:22.105
Just keep going.

19:22.211 --> 19:25.795
But isn't it against the rules to use
an abacus with one's tongue?

19:25.965 --> 19:28.175
I've never heard of such a thing.

19:36.434 --> 19:39.686
Muraoka-kun's hands were crippled.

19:39.687 --> 19:42.481
So he used to practice the abacus with his tongue.

19:42.940 --> 19:47.000
But because people laughed at him,
he wouldn't do it in public.

19:47.236 --> 19:53.513
Mr. Judge, please allow Muraoka-kun to complete
the rest of the round with his tongue.

19:53.993 --> 19:55.110
Please!

20:01.584 --> 20:06.505
There are no regulations prohibiting the
use of one's tongue during the contest.

20:06.798 --> 20:08.548
Please continue reading the problem.

20:09.175 --> 20:09.966
Yes, sir.

20:13.930 --> 20:15.722
Thank you

20:15.723 --> 20:17.142
Let's resume then.

20:17.433 --> 20:23.939
Please add 23,230,785

20:23.940 --> 20:27.108
plus 45,200,528.

20:30.154 --> 20:32.022
They're both correct.

20:35.493 --> 20:37.629
Let's continue the final round.

20:37.912 --> 20:39.093
Problem four.

20:39.168 --> 20:39.850
Ready.

20:40.039 --> 20:41.513
Keep going, Eiji.

20:41.958 --> 20:42.749
Don't give up!

20:43.376 --> 20:49.089
Please add 78,695,528

20:49.090 --> 20:51.633
plus 48,65...

20:53.010 --> 20:53.993
Doc!

20:54.303 --> 20:56.513
Doc!

20:56.961 --> 20:58.932
Doc, what's the matter?

20:58.933 --> 21:00.704
- You're spacing out.

21:00.851 --> 21:02.769
Oh, it's nothing.

21:02.896 --> 21:04.521
That's weird.

21:05.398 --> 21:06.982
Hey, look, look!

21:06.983 --> 21:10.277
Master showed me how to use it.

21:13.739 --> 21:17.026
One plus one is two!

21:17.159 --> 21:19.619
Oh! It went away!

21:21.038 --> 21:24.582
It'll take you a hundred years before you
can compete in an abacus contest.

21:24.583 --> 21:26.876
An abacus contest?

21:26.877 --> 21:29.004
I'm pretty good at it.

21:29.005 --> 21:30.427
Watch this...

21:31.048 --> 21:31.923
Sharaku!

21:33.217 --> 21:34.968
I knew you'd be here!

21:34.969 --> 21:36.720
Onee-chan!

21:36.721 --> 21:38.179
Where's your homework?!

21:38.723 --> 21:40.836
I was learning how to use an abacus.

21:41.100 --> 21:43.643
I was thinking of doing my homework with it.

21:43.807 --> 21:44.975
I see.

21:45.229 --> 21:47.272
Then go ahead and use it.

21:49.400 --> 21:52.994
You can't have dinner until you've finished
all of your calculations with that abacus.

21:55.197 --> 21:56.750
Thank you very much.

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
being heated up by you,

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
so much that I change color

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
I couldn't be happier

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.983 --> 23:33.917
How does it taste?

23:28.983 --> 23:33.916
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.057 --> 24:15.128
Tragedy in the High Technology Room

23:45.134 --> 23:45.701
There.

23:48.039 --> 23:50.395
We're proud to present to you this building, built
and equipped with the latest technology.

23:50.445 --> 23:52.095
The fire can no longer get to us.

23:52.362 --> 23:53.068
Oh?

23:53.229 --> 23:54.446
Open this door!

23:54.684 --> 23:56.245
The air is being sucked out.

23:56.614 --> 23:58.470
Largo!

23:58.725 --> 24:00.581
If we cut the cord inside this wall...

24:00.725 --> 24:03.701
I can't give up without trying.

24:04.035 --> 24:04.585
I can't breathe!

24:04.885 --> 24:06.846
Damn, I'm at my limit.

24:07.112 --> 24:09.173
We're going to suffocate in this room.

24:11.700 --> 24:14.422
Next Karte - Tragedy in the High Technology Room.

24:16.097 --> 24:17.856
Karte NG...

24:19.047 --> 24:20.714
I knew you'd be here!

24:20.715 --> 24:21.507
Onee-chan!
